        "original_id": "6def222a-5e7b-5532-9330-d90dc52d1eee",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: George Albert Smith Sr., Wong Jing\n- Organizations: The Church of Jesus Christ of Latter-day Saints (LDS Church)\n- Places: Salt Lake Valley\n- Monuments: This is the Place Monument\n- Roles: LDS Church president, film director, producer, actor, presenter, screenwriter\n- Events: Dedication of This is the Place Monument, pioneers entering the Salt Lake Valley\n\nFacts:\n- George Albert Smith Sr. was born on April 4, 1870, and he was an American religious leader.\n- George Albert Smith Sr. served as the eighth president of The Church of Jesus Christ of Latter-day Saints.\n- Wong Jing was born on 3 May 1955, and he is a Hong Kong film director, producer, actor, presenter, and screenwriter.\n- This is the Place Monument was dedicated by LDS Church President George Albert Smith on 24 July 1947.\n- The dedication of This is the Place Monument marked the hundredth anniversary of the pioneers entering the Salt Lake Valley.\n- George Albert Smith Sr. died on April 4, 1951.",
